title: Coppicing
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Cut a tree off near the ground and it sends up a ring of new shoots. Wait some years, cut the shoots, and it does it again.

The tree isn't killed. A coppiced hazel can be cut over and over for centuries.

It is good for the woodland too. Each cutting lets light reach the ground for a few years, and different plants and animals move in.

The thin rods are what [[Sebastian Cox]] builds with. See [[Products of Silviculture Suent chair]], [[Silviculture]].
